{"lines": ["Next, a body on a beach. Adelaide, South Australia. The first of December, 1948, at Somerton Park. A man, never identified.", "Months later, in a hidden fob pocket of his trousers, police found a tiny rolled scrap of paper. Two words, printed: Tamam Shud. It means \"ended\". It was torn from the last page of a book of poems, the Rubaiyat of Omar Khayyam.", "Police found the copy it came from. In the back, faint indentations. Five lines of capital letters, the second line struck out.", "In 1978, Defence Department cryptographers looked at it. Their verdict. There were not enough symbols for a satisfactory answer, and the text might even be meaningless.", "Derek Abbott's team concluded that the letters are probably the first letters of words. In 2014, John Rehling's analysis supported initials of some English text.", "Initials of a sentence you do not have is a lock with no key.", "In 2022, Abbott and a genealogist claimed the man was Carl Webb, using DNA from his hair. South Australia Police have not verified it.", "Rule six. Some messages are too short to be solved. Do not force an answer."], "words": [["Next,", 0.0, 0.28], ["a", 0.28, 0.5], ["body", 0.5, 0.74], ["on", 0.74, 1.08], ["a", 1.08, 1.16], ["beach.", 1.16, 1.4], ["Adelaide,", 2.1, 2.28], ["South", 2.72, 2.9], ["Australia.", 2.9, 3.5], ["The", 3.5, 3.773], ["first", 3.773, 4.047], ["of", 4.047, 4.32], ["December,", 4.32, 4.98], ["1948,", 4.98, 6.36], ["at", 6.36, 7.16], ["Somerton", 7.16, 7.54], ["Park.", 7.54, 7.92], ["A", 8.44, 8.58], ["man,", 8.58, 8.88], ["never", 8.88, 9.38], ["identified.", 9.38, 10.16], ["Months", 10.86, 11.16], ["later,", 11.16, 11.56], ["in", 11.88, 11.93], ["a", 11.93, 12.0], ["hidden", 12.0, 12.14], ["fob", 12.14, 12.46], ["pocket", 12.46, 13.0], ["of", 13.0, 13.14], ["his", 13.14, 13.24], ["trousers,", 13.24, 13.46], ["police", 14.22, 14.44], ["found", 14.44, 14.74], ["a", 14.74, 14.88], ["tiny", 14.88, 15.22], ["rolled", 15.22, 15.54], ["scrap", 15.54, 16.02], ["of